 the value $y=2$ is NOT a valid output of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at this endpoint." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489242 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489242 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489242 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489242 #edb/ref 1069 "q-236716" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489242 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489242 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6a/6a837faad775bb111760b2e90920c0490c42473c77f74f8be7a46271df154d97.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)<$\n{{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489242 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92babace-3fcf-5d4a-8789-c7e1f3a12026" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489242 #edb/ref 1074 "We find the ranges of the individual pieces and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (-3,1)$ is $(-1,3)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [1,4)$ is $\\{1\\}$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $(-1,3)\\cup \\{1\\}=(-1,3),$ which can also be written as \n\n$$\n-1<f(x)<3.\n$$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the values $y=-1$ and $y=3$ are NOT valid outputs of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use \"less than\" $(<)$ instead of \"less than or equal to\" $(\\le )$ at these endpoints." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489305 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489305 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "272370e5-078e-580c-b640-0e722fe6c08f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489305 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489226 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489316 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489316 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4667bb2a-2002-535b-abeb-65e5c33b3eb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489316 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 